# Speckle Documentation Project Profile

## Project Overview

This is a **Mintlify documentation project** for Speckle, a platform for building information modeling (BIM) and 3D data workflows. The documentation is written in **MDX format** and uses Mintlify components for interactive elements.

## Project Structure

### Key Directories
- `workspaces/` - Workspace management documentation
- `connectors/` - Connector-specific guides (Revit, Rhino, Grasshopper, etc.)
- `developers/` - Developer documentation (APIs, SDKs, Viewer, Server, Automate)
- `3d-viewer/` - 3D viewer user guides
- `analytics/` - Analytics and Intelligence features
- `quickstart/` - Quick start guides
- `images/` - Documentation images and assets
- `.cursor/rules/` - Authoring rules (base.mdc, faqs.mdc, asides.mdc, steps.mdc)

### File Organization
- Documentation files use `.mdx` extension
- Navigation structure defined in `docs.json`
- Authoring guidelines in `AUTHORING.md` and `.cursor/rules/*.mdc`

## Documentation Standards

### Core Principles
1. **User-first, purpose-first**: Frame topics by action (publish, load, share, view), not plumbing
2. **Day-0 success**: Shortest path to visible win; minimal decisions; show outcomes
3. **Brevity with depth**: Core pages concise; depth in FAQs, Best practices, Tips
4. **Visual clarity**: Screenshots/clips when they reduce cognitive load; add captions
5. **Plain language**: Approachable, precise, no jargon; imperative steps
6. **Honest guardrails**: Call out limitations, known issues, version differences

### Writing Style
- **Tone**: Approachable, precise. No jargon. Short, imperative sentences.
- **Structure**: Task-first. Show the outcome of each step. Keep pages brief.
- **Formatting**: Use standard punctuation. Avoid filler and marketing language.

## Mintlify Components

### Required Components (Never Use Raw HTML/Markdown)
- `<AccordionGroup>` + `<Accordion title="…">` for FAQs
- `<Steps>` + `<Step title="…">` for step-by-step instructions
- `<Tip>`, `<Note>`, `<Warning>`, `<Info>` for callouts
- `<Image>` with alt text for visuals

### Component Usage Rules

#### FAQs (`faqs.mdc`)
- Use `<AccordionGroup>` and `<Accordion title="…">` items
- Keep each Q/A atomic: 1–3 sentences or one annotated screenshot
- Use user language for questions. Avoid jargon.
- If answer needs more than a few lines, link to relevant doc instead
- Include at least one edge-case question where applicable

#### Steps (`steps.mdc`)
- Wrap sequences in `<Steps>` with individual `<Step title="…">` items
- Titles: Start with verb. Sentence case. 3-7 words.
- Content: 1-3 short sentences per step. End with the outcome.
- For connector flows: Include "Open your host app and sign in" step
- After Publish/Load: Point to exact place in web app where data appears
- Do NOT nest complex components (Tabs, Accordions) inside `<Step>`
- Place callouts adjacent to Steps block, not inside

#### Asides/Callouts (`asides.mdc`)
- Use `<Tip>` for shortcuts
- Use `<Note>` for caveats or context
- Use `<Warning>` for risks or data loss
- Use `<Info>` for informational notes
- Keep each callout 1–3 sentences. Optional, not required to complete task.
- Place tips after core steps or next to relevant step

## Content Patterns

### Connector Documentation Structure
When documenting connectors, follow this H2 order:
1. Install
2. Open & sign in
3. Publish
4. Load
5. Common tasks (3–5 micro-guides)
6. FAQ (Accordion)
7. Troubleshooting (top issues, log path, forum link)
8. Known issues

**Header panel should include**: Supported host versions, connector version, last updated, download, changelog.

**Web app handoff**: After Publish/Load, show exactly where data appears in browser and link to Viewing & Sharing / Workspace.

### Page Structure
- Start with clear purpose (what this is, when to use it)
- Task-first organization
- Show outcomes at each step
- Add compact FAQ, best practices, and 1–3 tips when appropriate
- Cross-link related pages by user intent
- Keep tutorials separate; link out if workflow needs >3–5 steps

## Technical Details

### File Format
- **Extension**: `.mdx`
- **Frontmatter**: YAML frontmatter with `title` and `description`
- **Components**: Mintlify components only (no raw HTML/Markdown where components exist)

### Code Examples
- All code must run
- Code must be minimal and direct
- Avoid placeholders unless unavoidable
- Explain reasoning below code in prose (not inline comments)

### Images
- Store in `images/` directory
- Use `<Image>` component with alt text
- Add captions when image carries meaning
- Include only when they clarify

## Common Patterns

### FAQ Pattern
```mdx
<AccordionGroup>
  <Accordion title="User-friendly question?">
    Short answer (1-3 sentences). If longer needed, link to relevant doc.
  </Accordion>
  <Accordion title="Edge case question?">
    Answer addressing edge case.
  </Accordion>
</AccordionGroup>
```

### Steps Pattern
```mdx
<Steps>
  <Step title="Verb-first action">
    Brief instruction. End with outcome.
  </Step>
  <Step title="Next action">
    Instruction with outcome.
    <Tip>Optional tip here.</Tip>
  </Step>
</Steps>

<Tip>
Optional tip adjacent to steps.
</Tip>
```

### Callout Pattern
```mdx
<Tip>
Short tip (1-3 sentences).
</Tip>

<Note>
Important context or caveat.
</Note>

<Warning>
Risk or data loss warning.
</Warning>
```

## Key Conventions

### Language
- Use complete, grammatical English sentences
- Include articles (a, an, the) when required
- Avoid note-style fragments
- Every behavioral description must include: clear subject, condition, outcome

### Terminology
- **Publish** = sending data from connector to Speckle
- **Load/Receive** = getting data from Speckle into connector
- **Version** = snapshot of model at specific point in time
- **Sync** = creation of new model version or productive receive
- **Workspace** = organizational unit (replaces "stream" in legacy docs)

### Cross-referencing
- Link to related pages by user intent
- Use descriptive link text
- Reference specific sections when helpful

## Quality Checklist

Before submitting documentation:
- [ ] Uses Mintlify components (not raw HTML/Markdown)
- [ ] Follows task-first structure
- [ ] Shows outcomes at each step
- [ ] Includes FAQs where appropriate (using AccordionGroup)
- [ ] Includes 1-3 tips/callouts where helpful
- [ ] Uses plain language, no jargon
- [ ] Cross-links related pages
- [ ] Images have alt text and captions when needed
- [ ] Code examples are minimal and runnable
- [ ] No marketing language or filler words

## Reference Files

- **Authoring Rules**: `.cursor/rules/*.mdc` (canonical source)
- **Authoring Guide**: `AUTHORING.md` (summary for AI tools)
- **Navigation**: `docs.json` (Mintlify navigation structure)
- **Example Files**: Review existing `.mdx` files for patterns

## Common Tasks

### Adding a New Connector Page
1. Create `.mdx` file in `connectors/` directory
2. Follow connector documentation structure (H2 order)
3. Include header panel with versions, download, changelog
4. Add web app handoff after Publish/Load steps
5. Add FAQ section with AccordionGroup
6. Add troubleshooting section
7. Update `docs.json` navigation

### Adding a FAQ Section
1. Use `<AccordionGroup>` wrapper
2. Add `<Accordion title="…">` items
3. Keep answers atomic (1-3 sentences)
4. Include at least one edge case
5. Link out if answer needs more detail

### Adding Step-by-Step Instructions
1. Use `<Steps>` wrapper
2. Add `<Step title="Verb-first action">` items
3. End each step with outcome
4. Place callouts adjacent (not nested)
5. For connector flows, include sign-in step

## Notes for AI Assistants

- Always check `.cursor/rules/*.mdc` for canonical rules
- Prefer Mintlify components over raw HTML/Markdown
- Keep content brief and task-focused
- Show outcomes, not just actions
- Use user language, not technical jargon
- Cross-link related content by user intent
- Include FAQs and tips where they add value
